Build the pinned Conan third-party recipes under Debian 13's gcc 14.

Upstream builds the 3.0 line with gcc 12 (its Ubuntu 22.04 builder image).
gcc 14 turns -Wincompatible-pointer-types into an error in C sources of the
recipes the line pins (libunwind's aarch64 sources tripped it on the 2.6 line);
the C++ side already force-includes <cstdint> upstream. scripts/3rdparty_build.sh
exports the compiler flags for every recipe and overwrites whatever the
environment set, so the waiver is spliced into that export.

Upstream script: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/blob/v3.0.1/scripts/3rdparty_build.sh
gcc 14 porting notes: https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-14/porting_to.html

diff --git a/scripts/3rdparty_build.sh b/scripts/3rdparty_build.sh
index eaa7de3..8f405ba 100644
--- a/scripts/3rdparty_build.sh
+++ b/scripts/3rdparty_build.sh
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ unset DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
 # Enable parallel downloads for faster dependency resolution
 export CONAN_CPU_COUNT=${CONAN_CPU_COUNT:-$(nproc 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.logicalcpu 2>/dev/null || echo 4)}
 export CXXFLAGS="-Wno-error=address -Wno-error=deprecated-declarations -include cstdint"
-export CFLAGS="-Wno-error=address -Wno-error=deprecated-declarations"
+export CFLAGS="-Wno-error=address -Wno-error=deprecated-declarations -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types"
 # LLVM from Homebrew doesn't set TARGET_OS_OSX=1 (unlike Apple's clang), which causes
 # macOS SDK headers to exclude macOS-specific APIs (SecImportExport, SCPreferences, etc.).
 # This fixes aws-c-cal, c-ares, and other packages that depend on macOS Security/SystemConfig APIs.
